    "messages": [
      {
        "id": "mvxve0axlnj0p",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "万瓶桥的雾贴着鞋面，像一层没有干透的浆糊。\n\n我站在东号窗外，指尖捏着一枚不该出现在我袖里的十七号旧签。窗内，裴算的朱砂笔悬在名册空白处，笔尖落下去，我的名字就会被抹去；笔尖抬起来，我就还能在这座城里再赖一个月。\n\n他忽然问：“你叫什么？”\n\n阿枣在桥边掀开汤锅，白气遮住了半张脸。她没有看我，只把一把盐粒撒进锅里，像在给什么人留记号。更远的桥腹下，有一串红泥脚印钻进黑暗，鞋跟的泥里混着碎蜡和人血。\n\n我的腕骨忽然一凉。残墨从袖口里探出半团黑，贴着我的皮肤，眼睛浅浅发亮。\n\n“你原来那一页，被人撕了。”它小声说，“这里少了一大笔。你要是愿意，我可以替你改一笔。只是改完以后，欠下的东西会自己找回来。”\n\n桥头的午钟尚未响。城里已经有四拨人在找一张没有主人的名字。有人想拿它洗白，有人想拿它杀人，有人想拿它换一整座城。\n\n而我只需要先回答裴算这一句——\n\n“你叫什么？”",
        "timestamp": 1793539968009
      },
      {
        "id": "mvxwrcorhsb61",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "我把旧签推到裴算面前，问：这枚签是谁的？",
        "displayContent": "我把旧签推到裴算面前，问：这枚签是谁的？",
        "timestamp": 1793542270203
      },
      {
        "id": "mvxwrct7pbrtt",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "我把签推过去。石台湿，签子在台面上滑出半寸，停在朱砂笔尖下方，像一枚自己送上门的证据。\n\n裴算没有伸手。\n\n他看那签的眼神，跟看一只还活着的虫子一样——先数了一遍它的腿，才决定要不要碰。左手仍藏在袖里，右手把那本名册翻过来，压住，动作很轻。\n\n“照规矩，签不离窗。”\n\n“那它怎么在我袖子里？”\n\n雾从他背后漫过来，把东号窗的铜铃也浸得发闷。我盯着他，看清了三件事：签的边不是剪的，是撕的，撕口起毛，毛里嵌着陈年的纸筋；签角有一枚半个朱砂指印，罗纹断在一道旧疤上；他右手中指的指腹，就在我眼前，也有一道同样的断纹。\n\n他刚才用左手压下名册，可袖口抖了一下——那截青灰布面上，凭空多了一小点红。他摸过自己的签。两枚，都还在。\n\n所以这第三枚不是他的。可这第三枚，是他亲手经过的。\n\n“这不是我这里出去的。”他说得太快了。\n\n我没接话，只把那枚签翻了个面，念出上面那个字：“十七。”\n\n他从喉咙里咽了一口气，那口抵在舌根，没落下去。这一下比追问“是谁的”更管用——他怕的不是我问名字，他怕我念数字。\n\n阿枣在桥头忽然撒了一把盐,盐粒落在青石上,噼啪地跳。我腕骨上一凉，残墨醒了，从袖口探出半团黑，把脸凑到台沿，去舔那些跳过来的盐末，舔得极其专注，像在替我占一个没人要的位置。\n\n“东号窗的号，”裴算终于开口，声音放软，客气得让人起鸡皮，“一签一人，签在，人就在册上。这枚——”他停了停，改口，“这位小友，你把它推到我面前，是要我做什么呢？照规矩，我只能给你一碗热水，让你坐着想一想。”\n\n他改口了。方才还是“你叫什么”，现在叫“小友”。\n\n他把左手从袖里抽了出来，我第一次看见那只手：少了半截小指，断处被朱砂填平成一片钝红。他从那只手里数出几张通钞，压在台角，不多不少，正好十七张，边角压得很齐，像他练过很多次。\n\n“签我收回去，这句话当我没问。”他说，“你也别问。”\n\n铜铃响了一下。不是风。桥头雾里站了个人，鞋跟是红的，红泥一直沾到裤脚，站得极稳，像在等谁把窗关上。他没往这边看，可他那双鞋的方向，正对着东号窗。\n\n裴算也看见了他。他把名册往怀里收得更紧了些，然后伸手，把那枚签和那叠钱，一起往我这边推了半寸。",
        "timestamp": 1793542270363,
        "reasoning_content": "The player pushes the old tag toward Pei Suan and asks whose it is. Social triumph, perception triumph, stealth triumph. Knowledge failure though. So they can't identify the name from lore, but they can read Pei Suan's reaction perfectly.\n\nLet me write a scene: the tag slides across the wet stone sill. Pei Suan's reaction. Perception triumph — I read everything: the smear of cinnabar, the two 17-tags in his sleeve, the way his left hand (hidden in sleeve) is the one that flinches. Social triumph — I press him, get a real concession/hold over him. Give a爽点: I catch him, force him to write something, or extract a name/fact.\n\nKnowledge failure — I don't know whose the tag is, or the lore detail wrong. So maybe I misread what the tag means, or I can't recall the numbering system. But I can still get something.\n\nLet me also include 残墨 eating salt, and 阿枣.\n\nLet's craft: the tag is a 十七号签 — Pei Suan has two in his kit. So this is a third? Or the tag is one of his own, meaning the tag is issued from the window. The tag itself—if I don't know whose it is, maybe the answer is: the tag has no name, only a number, and the number is burned. But it's a \"旧签\" — old tag.\n\nPerception triumph: I see the salt on his cuff, the fact his left hand is missing a fingertip? No — keep to existing kit: 指腹有洗不净的朱砂, 左手总藏在袖里.\n\nGive a爽点: I catch his tell — his left hand covers the 名册's corner where a page was torn; the torn page matches my tag. So the tag is a page-stub. Also 阿枣's salt hint.\n\nConsequence/echo: he makes a countermove — writes something in the ledger, or threatens quietly, or a runner leaves. Also should leave a physical change: maybe he flips the ledger shut and the window's 铜铃 rings, or someone in the queue behind me notices.\n\nAlso maybe he offers me something — since he's 胆小 and 怕丢官: he'd try to buy me. Let me have him slide 三十通钞? That's阿枣's goal — nice echo. Maybe he offers 十七通钞. Hmm, let me have him offer a bribe in 通钞 — that would be a爽点 (赚到钱) but the player hasn't decided. Better: I catch the tell, he stammers, and he does something concrete that I can use.\n\nLet me write 500-800 汉字. Grounded tone.\n\nStructure:\n1. Action result: tag pushed forward, the sound, his reaction.\n2. Perception triumph: details — the朱砂 thumbprint on the tag's edge matching his, or the tag's torn edge matching the ledger's torn stub.\n3. Social triumph: I speak, he cracks; he says something he shouldn't.\n4. New change: he does something — rings the closing bell early? Or a boy is sent running. And 阿枣's salt.\n\nLet me make the爽点 line: \"照规矩，签不离窗。\" and I answer something that pins him — like \"那它怎么在我袖里?\" and his hand goes white.\n\nAdd concrete fact established: the torn edge fits. So the tag is a torn-off corner of a ledger page — meaning the person's name was cut off. Good world texture.\n\nAnd a new change: he pulls the ledger away and shuts the shutter half — window closing early; also he says a name inadvertently: \"陆照夜\" — no, that's his fear trigger; if I mention 陆照夜 he looks for a scapegoat. Knowledge failure means I shouldn't necessarily know that. But I could press the tag and he mutters something. Let's have him blurt: \"这不是我这里出去的。\" — a lie, obvious. Echo: someone behind me in the queue (a woman with a 瓶 in her basket?) hears.\n\nAlso the 红泥脚印 — a runner in red mud shoes leaving, I notice (perception triumph) — the footprints go under the bridge; and now a figure in the mist at the bridge head wearing red-mud shoes, watching the window. That's a looming threat but not immediate.\n\nLet's write.\n\nAlso I should include a 爽点 explicitly:被迫改口 — 裴算 calls me something different, or he offers money.\n\nLet me write:\n\n---\n\n我把签推过去。石台湿...\n\nPei Suan doesn't touch it. 朱砂笔 stays up. He looks at it the way one looks at a live insect.\n\nThen: \"照规矩，签不离窗。\"\n\"那它怎么在我袖子里？\"\n\nHis left hand—hidden—moves. I see the fabric twitch, and a thumb of cinnabar smear appears at the cuff edge where he pressed it against his own wrist. Meaning: he counted his two tags and found them both there. So the third is not his.\n\nPerception triumph: the tag's edge is not cut, it's torn — and the tear matches the 名册's inner margin? I can't see the ledger's margin because he closes it. Hmm. Instead: 签上有半个朱砂指纹, the ridge pattern — and I've seen his fingers on the window's chipped rim, leaving prints. Match. So he did handle it.\n\nThen the tell: he says \"这不是我这里出去的\" too fast. And I note: the tag is numbered 十七 — and he has two 十七号签 in his sleeve, which is impossible by rules (一签一人). Wait, kit says 两枚十七号签. So he holds TWO spare 17 tags. If I don't know the rule (knowledge failure), I can still see two tags fall out.\n\nActually knowledge failure: I don't know what 十七号 means — whether it's a person's number, a window, a day, a seal. That's a nice gap: the number means nothing to me, but he flinches at it. Good.\n\nSo: \"十七\" — I say the number aloud and watch him; perversely, saying it costs him more than asking whose it is.\n\nThen he cracks: he tells me one true thing to get me to go: \"使君的四十六页，昨夜被剪了。\" Hmm, invent.\n\nBetter concrete concession: he admits the page was cut from the ledger, and offers me 十七通钞 to hand back the tag and say nothing. That's 赚到钱 (potential). And a name change: he starts calling me \"小友\" — the 改口 honor.\n\nEcho: he also writes something in the ledger as he says it — a note, and I see him write my description. And the bell. And the red-mud figure at the bridgehead.\n\nEnd with the hidden MOVEMENT comment.\n\nWord count ~700. Let's write it carefully in good Chinese prose.\n\nCareful not to decide for the player: don't have the player take the money. Just have Pei Suan put it on the sill. Player must decide.\n\nAlso 残墨 eating salt — 阿枣's salt scattered; 残墨 laps at salt on the sill. Small beat.\n\nWrite.",
        "sceneId": "001"
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0wn5ise5zx",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "你好",
        "displayContent": "你好",
        "timestamp": 1793549235510
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0wn7nvr2oi",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "我没有碰那叠钱。我只把签又往前推了半寸，推得让它压在钱上，两个东西一起压着，谁也走不了。\n\n“这个我不要。”我说，“我要他抽一份。”\n\n我的下巴朝雾里那个红泥鞋抬了抬。\n\n裴算的脸一下子白了。他指尖在桌面绷紧，十七张钞的边角被他压得翘起来又弹回去。他张了张嘴，那句“照规矩”卡在喉咙里，没吐出来——他明白这是什么意思：给编号的人，才配来问签。我让他把这个人叫过来，把问题当着三个人的面摊开。\n\n“你也想清楚了。”他声音很轻，带一点笑，“他要是抽中了，明天清册上就没有你这个人了。”\n\n“清册上本来就快没有我了。”我说，“你刚才自己讲的。”\n\n他含着的那口气勉强吐出去，左手缩回袖里，压着名册。就在这时候，残墨贴着台沿，忽然转过头去，冲着雾里那个人抽了抽鼻子，舔盐的劲头一下停了。\n\n“他鞋底不是红泥。”它小声说，声音又低又黏，“是蜡，混了人血。而且——他身上有味道。和你有的那种一样。”\n\n我腕骨一紧。它在说“少了一笔”，说的不是我。\n\n裴算没听见它，只顾把名册往案上一摆，扬声叫：“三十七号，过来抽。”声音稳得不像他自己的。\n\n雾里的人动了，却没有朝窗走来。他反手把什么东西往桥腹的黑暗里一推，从那儿传来一声极轻的、被人捂住嘴的闷响。然后他才迈开步子，来得很慢，鞋跟一点一点敲在青石上。他一边走一边抬手，把卷起的袖口放下来，把一只烫得起了水泡的手腕盖住。\n\n裴算的手在案上抖了。\n\n我看见了——这是他第一次真的抖。",
        "timestamp": 1793549235587,
        "sceneId": "002"
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0x0cp1wlsf",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "傻呀",
        "displayContent": "傻呀",
        "timestamp": 1793549252617
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0x0dqkh7xj",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "三十七号在人前站定，先不看名册，看我。\n\n他比我高半头，脸上没什么表情，烫得起泡的那只手垂在身侧，盖得严实。他身上的气味随着靠近漫过来，很淡，是蜡、汗，还有另一层东西——残墨说得没错，那层东西和我腕骨上的很像：纸被撕开以后留下的那种干涩。\n\n“让开点。”他说，“我要抽。”\n\n裴算把竹筒推出来，筒里的签哗啦啦响。三十七号伸手进去，不急，指尖在筒底摸了一圈，像在找某一枚特定的签。我看着他那只没盖住的手——食指和中指的关节上有一圈极细的、被丝线勒出来的印子，是长期绑着什么留下的。绑刀，或者是绑着别人的手。\n\n他抽出来了，往案上一放。十八号。\n\n裴算看了一眼，整个人松了半寸，嘴里“照规矩”三个字还没说完，就被三十七号自己截了。\n\n“十八号是空的。”三十七号把签推回去，声音平得很，“空号补签，得先交一份活人。裴录事，你今早交上去的那份——”他停了停，眼睛慢慢转到我脸上，“是你。还是他？”\n\n裴算的朱砂笔掉在名册上，洇开一团红。\n\n这一下，什么都通了。这枚十七号旧签不是三十七号的，是裴算的。今早他要往上交的那份“活人”，本来就是我。三十七号当着我念出来，不是为了帮我，是要掐住裴算的把柄，让他今天交不出名额——交不出，清籍院就得派人来查，一查，桥腹下那声被捂住的闷响就藏不住了。\n\n他在桥腹底下也留了一个人。\n\n我腕上残墨贴着台沿不动了，眼睛眯成两弯，“他身上缺的那一笔，是给别人的。”它说完就闭嘴了，爪子扒着台沿往桥腹的方向探。\n\n三十七号转过身来，第二次正视我，语气还那么平：“你叫什么？”",
        "timestamp": 1793549252654,
        "sceneId": "003"
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0xbi06o46g",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "我说不玩了",
        "displayContent": "我说不玩了",
        "timestamp": 1793549267064
      },
      {
        "id": "mvy0xbix7ndyl",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "“不玩了。”\n\n我把签和那叠钱一起推回去，推得它们撞到竹筒，哗啦一片。\n\n三十七号盯着我看了两息。他没怒，反而笑了一下，很浅。“不玩了，是哪种不玩？是把签收回去，还是把桥底下那个人也一块儿不管？”\n\n我心里一沉，却没应声。他这句不是问，是递刀。他知道桥腹下那声闷响我听见了。\n\n裴算倒是先动了。他一把把名册往怀里收，像要抢先定下今天清册的结局。可他收得太急，一张夹在两页中间的旧纸滑出来，飘到案角。纸上只有半行字，剩下一半显然是被人撕走的，纸边起毛，跟那枚十七号签的撕口一模一样。\n\n三十七号也看见了。\n\n“照规矩，”他慢慢开口,把声调拉得跟裴算常骗人时一个样，“撕页不补，这份名册作废。作废的名册，得送正堂验。”\n\n裴算的脸彻底没了血色。他转向我，那种客气终于压不住了，露出底下的东西：“小友，你今天这两个字，我可以当没听见。”他往前凑了半寸，“但名册要是送去了正堂，桥底下那个,还有你——别人可不会像我这样讲规矩。”\n\n桥头，阿枣忽然敲了两下汤锅沿。她没说话，只抬眼朝我这边瞟了一眼，又低下头去收拾摊子，收得比往常快了。她在赶我走，也在给自己关门。\n\n我腕上的残墨贴着台沿，一动不动了一会儿，然后轻轻说：“那半页，我知道在哪儿。是被人拿走的，不是被风吹走的。”它顿一顿，“他做的。”爪子朝三十七号的方向偏了一下。\n\n三十七号没有否认。他只是把那只烫起水泡的手背到身后，语气还是平的：“你想知道那半页去哪了，跟我走。你想把这件事交给正堂，那你也得先走出这座桥。”\n\n雾里，第一声午钟起了一半，闷闷地卡在铜里。桥头另有两双鞋走进了雾，不快，方向是清籍院正堂。",
        "timestamp": 1793549267097,
        "swipeSet": [
          {
            "id": "mvy0xg5o9ih7c",
